# WHAT IS THIS FILE?
# .gitattributes lets you tell git to treat specific files or paths
# differently than git's defaults — for example, marking generated code so
# GitHub doesn't count it in language statistics, marking vendored
# (third-party, not-written-by-us) code the same way, or telling git to use
# a custom "diff driver" (a smarter way of showing what changed) for files
# whose normal text diff would be unreadable, like encrypted files. Git
# reads this file automatically; you don't run it or include it anywhere.

# `#` starts a comment in a .gitattributes file, same as in git's other
# config-style files — ignored by git, here for human readers.
# This line points to git's own documentation for the full attributes
# syntax, in case you need something beyond what's demonstrated below.
# See https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes for more about git attribute files.

# Blank line — purely visual separation between sections.

# Mark the database schema as having been generated.
# `db/schema.rb` is the path being tagged (relative to the project root, no
# leading slash needed here since gitattributes matches paths, not just
# root-anchored ones the way .gitignore patterns sometimes are).
# `linguist-generated` is a GitHub-specific attribute recognized by
# GitHub Linguist (the tool that powers the "language breakdown" bar you
# see on a repo's GitHub page, and that decides which files show up by
# default in pull request diffs). Marking schema.rb as generated tells
# GitHub "a machine wrote this file (via `rails db:schema:dump`), don't
# count it toward the app's Ruby percentage, and collapse it by default in
# PR diffs since a human didn't hand-author these changes."
db/schema.rb linguist-generated

# Blank separator line.

# Mark any vendored files as having been vendored.
# `vendor/*` matches everything directly inside the vendor/ directory (the
# `*` wildcard stands in for any file or folder name at that level).
# `linguist-vendored` is another GitHub Linguist attribute meaning "this is
# third-party code we didn't write, just copied in" — like linguist-
# generated, it excludes these files from the repo's language statistics
# and de-emphasizes them in diffs, since changes here aren't this team's
# original work.
vendor/* linguist-vendored
# `config/credentials/*.yml.enc` matches any encrypted per-environment
# credentials file (Rails' pattern for secrets scoped to one environment,
# e.g. config/credentials/production.yml.enc). `diff=rails_credentials`
# assigns a custom "diff driver" named rails_credentials to these files —
# normally `git diff` shows line-by-line text changes, but that's useless
# (and would leak nothing meaningful) for encrypted ciphertext, so this
# tells git to instead invoke a special diff tool that can decrypt-and-diff
# the readable contents. (The actual rails_credentials diff driver itself
# is registered separately, typically in Rails' generated .git/config or
# global git config — this line only assigns the driver's name to these
# paths, it doesn't define what the driver does.)
config/credentials/*.yml.enc diff=rails_credentials
# `config/credentials.yml.enc` is the single main (non-per-environment)
# encrypted credentials file Rails generates by default — same
# rails_credentials diff driver applied, for the same reason.
config/credentials.yml.enc diff=rails_credentials
